{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 29, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Adventure in Japan**\n\nJapan was everything I dreamed—vibrant, orderly, and endlessly fascinating. My trip began in **Tokyo**, where neon lights and towering skyscrapers gave way to quiet alleys lined with tiny izakayas. I lost myself in **Shibuya Crossing**, then escaped to **Asakusa**, where the scent of incense and the glow of **Senso-ji Temple** welcomed me. A stop at **Tsukiji Market** for sushi so fresh it practically swam off my plate sealed the deal.\n\nFrom Tokyo, I ventured to **Kyoto**, where ancient temples blended seamlessly with cherry blossoms. **Fushimi Inari Shrine’s** countless red torii gates stretched into the hills, while **Kinkaku-ji** (the Golden Pavilion) shimmered like a palace from a storybook. Tea in a traditional **machiya** house sipped slowly, the ritual as soothing as the matcha.\n\nA bullet train whisked me to **Osaka**, where street food beckoned. Takoyaki and okonomiyaki became my new obsessions, washed down with cold Asahi beer. Nearby **Nara** stole my heart—wild deer bowing for treats and **Todai-ji Temple**, home to the world’s largest bronze Buddha.\n\nMy last stop was **Hiroshima**, a place of history and hope. The **Peace Memorial Park**, with its haunting Cenotaph and Children’s Peace Monument, reminded me of both sorrow and resilience.\n\nJapan left me breathless—where every meal was a masterpiece, every temple a story, and every train ride on time. Already, I’m counting the days until I return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4.7801782784517854e-05}, {"token": " Adventure", "logprob": -0.8805687427520752}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.08243269473314285}, {"token": " Ja